<section class="section" id="process">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div class="kicker">Adoptions · Process</div>
      <h2>How the adoption process works</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Adopting a pet is a meaningful commitment. Follow the steps below to
        learn how to apply, what documents to bring and how your application is
        assessed.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="poster-card">
        <img
          alt="Tshwane SPCA adoption process information poster"
          class="poster"
          decoding="async"
          loading="lazy"
          src="/assets/adoption-process.jpg"
        />
        <div class="poster-actions">
          <button data-view="process" type="button">🔎 Enlarge poster</button
          ><a
            download="adoption-process.jpg"
            href="/assets/adoption-process.jpg"
            >⬇ Save poster</a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Adoption process – step by step</h3>
        <div class="steps adoption-steps">
          <div class="step">
            <h3>1. Visit a branch and meet your pet</h3>
            <p>
              Visit our Waltloo or Centurion Branch and spend time with the dog
              or cat you are interested in adopting. Our team can help you learn
              more about the animal.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>2. Complete the adoption application</h3>
            <p>
              Fill in an adoption application and pay the
              <strong>non-refundable reservation deposit</strong>. If your
              application is approved, the deposit is deducted from the full
              adoption fee.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>3. Arrange a meet-and-greet (dogs)</h3>
            <p>
              If you are adopting a dog and already have one or more dogs at
              home, please bring your dogs to the branch for a supervised
              meet-and-greet to assess compatibility.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>4. Provide the necessary documents</h3>
            <p>
              Before a home inspection can take place, please provide
              <strong>proof of identity</strong> and
              <strong>proof of residence</strong>. If you rent, include a
              <strong>letter of permission from your property owner</strong>. If
              you live in a complex or estate, provide
              <strong>written permission from the body corporate</strong>.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>5. Pre-home inspection</h3>
            <p>
              Once your documents have been submitted and any required
              compatibility tests have been completed, an SPCA Inspector will
              conduct a pre-home inspection.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>6. Inspector approval</h3>
            <p>
              All adoptions are
              <strong>subject to SPCA Inspector approval</strong>. Once
              approved, the branch will explain the remaining arrangements for
              welcoming your new companion home.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="adoption-fees-note adoption-fees-panel">
          <h3 class="adoption-fees-title">Adoption fees &amp; enquiries</h3>
          <p class="adoption-fees-intro">
            For <strong>current adoption fees</strong>, please call the branch
            directly. Adoption includes sterilisation, microchipping,
            age-appropriate vaccinations and deworming.
          </p>
          <p class="adoption-fees-list">
            <strong>Waltloo Branch:</strong>
            <a href="tel:+27128035219">012 803 5219</a><br /><strong
              >Centurion Branch:</strong
            >
            <a href="tel:+27126645644">012 664 5644</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
